# K10 - "No memory may be lost". Kata sandbox sketch (plan section 3.6).
# [K10-nn] sketch IDs are recognised by validate_architecture / trace and ignored by the
# CI adl-coverage gate. Never [TR-*]; promotion is decided only at K12 (architecture/REVIEW.md).
DESCRIPTION K10 - the paths where a memory's only copy can be truncated, dropped or mistaken
CATEGORY Data
NAMESPACE TrK10NS
DEFINE SYSTEM Total Recall K10 Sandbox AS trk10
    DEFINE COMPONENT Memory File Writers AS writers
    DEFINE COMPONENT Provenance AS provenance
    DEFINE COMPONENT Supersede Archive AS archive

# Course pp. 35-36: reconcile so that nothing received is lost. The .md files are the only copy of a
# memory's content. TR-W3 orders .md before index, TR-D11 archives on a force-overwrite. What remains:
# the hook writes tmp + rename, the server writes in place. A crash mid-write can truncate the only copy.
# That is a decided exemption (BACKLOG), so the check pins the pairing both ways.
ASSERT(Memory File Writers: raw memory-file writes exist only together with a backlog exemption that has a trigger, and the exemption goes when the writes do) # [K10-01]

# A memory the PreCompact hook extracted and one an agent stored on purpose differ in trust and in how
# to prune them. The server stamps the session; the extractor writes sessions: [] and no origin.
ASSERT(Provenance: every memory writer stamps a session or an origin) # [K10-02]

# TR-D11 archives the prior body before a force-overwrite, but the archive is best-effort. That is
# defensible only if a failed archive is recorded; today the catch is empty.
ASSERT(Supersede Archive: a failed archive of the prior body is recorded, never swallowed) # [K10-03]

# Not re-asserted, answered with existing evidence (answers.md): .md before index (TR-W3), supersede
# archive and supersededAt (TR-D11), atomic index files (TR-W1), org reconciliation (TR-W9, TR-W10),
# the single-writer index.json note (plugins/total-recall/CLAUDE.md, mergeRuntimeFieldsFromDisk).
